WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:01.442
Do you watch CSI?

00:00:01.442 --> 00:00:02.522
Law and Order?

00:00:02.522 --> 00:00:03.640
NCIS?

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.620
I like how those crime shows use

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.660
modern science to get the bad guy.

00:00:08.662 --> 00:00:09.720
Rob's prints

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:12.380
are all over Singer's convertible.

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:15.654
The pollen that was in Petty Officer Bick's lungs

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.980
is found only one place on earth.

00:00:17.980 --> 00:00:19.936
People who watch these shows

00:00:19.936 --> 00:00:22.800
believe that this is how it's really done.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.360
It's not?

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.540
It's not.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:26.497
Former detective Harry Houck's annoyed

00:00:26.497 --> 00:00:27.630
that the TV shows make

00:00:27.630 --> 00:00:30.220
forensic science look infallible.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:34.260
And you watch a detective get down and look at a body

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:35.180
and touch it

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.720
"he's been dead for three hours now,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:40.480
he ate dinner four hours ago."

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.800
I can't do that.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:44.480
On TV, experts identify the killer

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.240
by his bite mark.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.597
A little 3D magic for clarity

00:00:48.597 --> 00:00:50.060
and I give you the

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.740
killer's incisors.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:52.725
In real life, experts

00:00:52.725 --> 00:00:55.860
claim they can identify criminals that way.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.920
Swinton was convicted and sentenced

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.120
to 60 years in prison based on testimony

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.440
that bite marks found on the victim

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:03.940
were his.

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:07.760
The TV show Cold Case Files covered the trial,

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.960
in which Alfred Swinton was convicted

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.520
because this so-called bite mark expert said

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.860
Swinton's teeth matched a bite on the victim.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:18.520
When the models of the teeth

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.100
were laid onto the bite mark,

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.520
it was a perfect match.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:24.640
The expert explained he's a neutral scientist.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:26.900
A forensic scientist is not on the side

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.720
of the prosecution or the defense.

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.500
We look at the evidence

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:31.680
and we make sure

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:33.705
that if we're going to make a decision,

00:01:33.705 --> 00:01:34.380
it's going to

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.457
be a truthful decision.

00:01:35.457 --> 00:01:36.940
The doctor was just wrong.

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:37.799
He was just wrong because

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:39.307
it's an unreliable technique.

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:40.451
It looks like science.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:41.080
It does.

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:42.540
They're in white lab coats,

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.820
they sound very authoritative,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:44.660
but they're full of it.

00:01:44.660 --> 00:01:45.860
Lawyer Chris Fabricant

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.720
helped get Swinton freed from jail

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.680
by doing a DNA test.

00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:50.909
New DNA evidence shows

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:51.780
he had nothing to do

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.420
with the 1991 murder of Carla Terry.

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:57.441
Tonight Alfred Swinton's conviction was vacated

00:01:57.441 --> 00:01:58.726
and he's a free man.

00:01:58.726 --> 00:02:00.220
That's Chris Fabricant

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.780
celebrating with Swinton

00:02:01.780 --> 00:02:03.420
the day he was released.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.920
Bite marks is similar to you and I maybe

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:09.254
looking at a cloud and then I say to you,

00:02:09.254 --> 00:02:11.180
John doesn't that cloud

00:02:11.190 --> 00:02:12.840
look like a rabbit to you?

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:14.320
And you look at it and say, yeah Chris

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:15.880
I think that does look like a rabbit.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.960
But that kind of junk science

00:02:18.964 --> 00:02:21.380
puts innocent people in jail.

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:23.320
That's one or two people.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:25.540
Many more people are in jail

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:27.140
and we're supposedly safer

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:28.260
because of that.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.320
If you think that maybe even 1%

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:34.030
of convicted defendants may have been

00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:37.720
innocent, we have 2.6 million people in prison today

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.900
so we're not talking about a couple of people,

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.420
we're talking about

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:41.880
tens of thousands of people.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:44.020
But the people who use these techniques

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:45.400
they believe in it,

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:46.427
they're confident.

00:02:46.427 --> 00:02:47.700
Sure, they're confident.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.120
It's faith based science.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:51.000
The expert who got Swinton convicted

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.560
now admits he was wrong

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:55.480
but police still trust bite marks.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:58.020
Let's say one tooth is missing in the front so

00:02:58.020 --> 00:02:59.400
you got to look at that and you go,

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:02.300
your suspect's got one tooth missing in the front

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:03.540
that's pretty good.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:05.640
But then again, that's not enough.

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:08.160
Houck says he'd demand other evidence,

00:03:08.169 --> 00:03:09.769
but not all cops do.

00:03:09.769 --> 00:03:11.769
Especially if experts say

00:03:11.769 --> 00:03:14.032
they're sure someone's guilty.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:16.120
When they say so, you trust that.

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:17.020
Yes.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.820
But even fingerprint evidence isn't foolproof.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.020
The deadliest terror attack on Europe

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.480
since World War II.

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.880
When terrorists in Madrid killed 193 people,

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.000
the FBI found this

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:30.440
fingerprint on one of the terrorist's bags

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.010
and matched it to this fingerprint of a

00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:33.974
man in Oregon.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.100
An international investigation led to Brandon Mayfield.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:38.920
However,

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:41.140
two weeks after Mayfield's arrest,

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.299
Spanish investigators found the

00:03:43.299 --> 00:03:46.432
man to whom the fingerprint really belonged.

00:03:46.432 --> 00:03:48.069
FBI researchers claimed

00:03:48.069 --> 00:03:51.240
fingerprints are right more than 99% of the time,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.200
but that still leaves plenty of

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:54.745
wrongful convictions.

00:03:54.745 --> 00:03:57.669
Other technique are even less accurate.

00:03:57.669 --> 00:03:59.222
Carpet fiber evidence,

00:03:59.222 --> 00:04:00.200
gun tracing,

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.580
hair matching.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:03.340
Microscopic hair comparison evidence

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.540
has been admitted by courts for a century.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:08.457
In one case, it was a dog's hair.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.180
A dog hair was associated wrongfully

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:11.280
with a human hair.

00:04:11.280 --> 00:04:13.260
Since the turn of this century,

00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:16.040
there have been 75 wrongful convictions.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:18.600
Fabricant works for the Innocence Project.

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.020
By using more modern DNA evidence,

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:22.560
the project's lawyers have

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.760
helped free 191 innocent people.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.300
All these people

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:29.020
were wrongly jailed

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:32.000
based on so-called scientific evidence.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:34.080
Why do judges admit this stuff?

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.980
Why don't defense attorneys

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:37.240
get it thrown out?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:39.190
We all went to law school because

00:04:39.190 --> 00:04:40.380
we don't know science,

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:41.400
we don't know math,

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.400
and if somebody comes in with a white

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.300
lab coat and says,

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.520
I've been accredited by the American Board of Forensic

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.947
Odontology and I've been practicing for 20 years

00:04:47.947 --> 00:04:49.060
that's good enough for

00:04:49.060 --> 00:04:49.980
government work.

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.718
That shouldn't be the standard.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.160
Too much is at stake.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:54.800
Jurors tend to believe people who

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:56.620
courts call experts.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:58.920
But the experts often rely on

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:00.400
junk science.

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:03.080
Juries and judges should be much

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:04.140
more skeptical.

